  "explanation": "Since $g(x) = f(x-1)$ and $f(x) = x^2 + 8x + 15$, we have $g(x) = (x-1)^2 + 8(x-1) + 15$. Expanding yields $g(x) = x^2 - 2x + 1 + 8x - 8 + 15 = x^2 + 6x + 8$. Substituting $x = -2$ gives $g(-2) = (-2)^2 + 6(-2) + 8 = 4 - 12 + 8 = 0$.",
